{"tag":"8TFL","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2610.12819","version":"1","local":"head-1","file":"","number":"1.1","section":"sec-7","order":1,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"{\\em Let ${\\bf C} \\subset {\\bf F}_{q^m}^N$ be a $q^m$-ary $K$-dimensional linear code such that ${\\bf C}^{q-1}\\subset {\\bf F}_{q^m}^N$ is an intersecting code. We assume that there is an explicit $[n,m]_q$ minimal code in ${\\bf F}_q^n$. Then we can construct a minimal linear $[Nn,Km]_q$ code in ${\\bf F}_q^{Nn}$ explicitly.}","path":"source","confidence":"high","env":"head","item":"statement/theorem","head":"manual","number_from":"head","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"smaller-strong.tex","from":154,"to":154},"hash":"sha256:c39322da4ddd8b4af451e27b99ebf88e12cc93848a58cf3a9af12c13716902cd","minhash":"","census":"2610.12819v1#head-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
{"tag":"VPHY","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2610.12819","version":"1","local":"head-2","file":"","number":"1.2","section":"sec-7","order":2,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"{\\em Suppose that $q$ is an arbitrary prime power and $m \\geq 2$ is a positive integer. We assume that there exists an explicit $[n,2m]_q$ minimal code. Then we construct a sequence of strong blocking sets $S_i \\subset P({\\bf F}_q, k_i-1)$, where $k_i$ goes to the infinity, such that $$\\lim\\frac{|S_i|}{k_i}\\leq \\frac{n(q^m-1)(q-1)}{m(q^m-3)}.$$ Equivalently, we construct sequences of minimal $q$-ary codes with rate at least $\\frac{m(q^m-3)}{n(q-1)(q^m-1)}$ explcitly.}","path":"source","confidence":"high","env":"head","item":"statement/theorem","head":"manual","number_from":"head","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"smaller-strong.tex","from":157,"to":157},"hash":"sha256:5c868b726976320f2154b4ad0c5f7505bd35a97637430a82f7e8ea48a70d9fe5","minhash":"","census":"2610.12819v1#head-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
{"tag":"LTGN","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2610.12819","version":"1","local":"head-3","file":"","number":"1.1","section":"sec-7","order":3,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"{\\em For $q=2$, we construct a sequence of linear binary minimal codes with the rate $\\frac{145}{961} \\approx \\frac{1}{6.6276}$ explicitly.}","path":"source","confidence":"high","env":"head","item":"statement/corollary","head":"manual","number_from":"head","scope":"paper","proof_status":"elsewhere","origin":"own","span":{"file":"smaller-strong.tex","from":160,"to":160},"hash":"sha256:d1e42c93c9c14e5799ae9916574fe0d407494bd332c08f484afb1631649b1757","minhash":"","census":"2610.12819v1#head-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
{"tag":"CB8K","kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"2610.12819","version":"1","local":"head-4","file":"","number":"1.2","section":"sec-7","order":4,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"{\\em For $q=3$, we construct a sequence of linear trifferent (ternary minimal) codes with the rate $\\frac{1}{20}$ explicitly.}","path":"source","confidence":"high","env":"head","item":"statement/corollary","head":"manual","number_from":"head","scope":"paper","proof_status":"elsewhere","origin":"own","span":{"file":"smaller-strong.tex","from":166,"to":166},"hash":"sha256:2194fdea42f899dcf3fa189a8baae8dbc0617e3064f3bbf3a0719a064e3df625","minhash":"","census":"2610.12819v1#head-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
