{"tag":"ROKF","kind":"proof","paper":"2610.12819","version":"1","local":"head-21","file":"","section":"sec-9","order":21,"title":"Proof","body_md":"In the case of $q=5$, from the upper bound based on probabilistic argument, there is a linear $[36,4]_5$ minimal code. This code can be constructed explicitly, since the dimension is $4$. Using this code as an inner code, the result follows from Theorem 3.1.\\\\","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"head","item":"proof","head":"manual","scope":"paper","proves":"head-20","attach":3,"span":{"file":"smaller-strong.tex","from":238,"to":242},"hash":"sha256:248c7e948e54437c6dccdb3cdcde9ef5e0a387483ff0e19ae36bdce7fafd4741","minhash":"","census":"2610.12819v1#proof-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
{"tag":"AH87","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2610.12819","version":"1","local":"head-22","file":"","number":"4.1","section":"sec-10","order":22,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"{\\em Suppose that there exists an projective smooth irreducible curve defined over ${\\bf F}_{81}$\nof genus $g$. Let $N$ be the number of its ${\\bf F}_{81}$-rational points. Then we construct an explicit $[14(N-t),4(u-g+1)]_3$ trifferent code for $u \u003c \\frac{N-t}{2}.$}","path":"source","confidence":"high","env":"head","item":"statement/proposition","head":"manual","number_from":"head","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"smaller-strong.tex","from":266,"to":267},"hash":"sha256:eb9e31ed46f1f3f78da115ec437973537bfd0b13c4f83c0372742b026b9a2191","minhash":"","census":"2610.12819v1#head-16","extractor":"ax/v0.5.29"}
